<p><br></p>
<h1 id=3D"ApplicationStatusOperationalization-ImpPoints">Imp Points</h1>
<ol>
 <li data-uuid=3D"30953506-e0e4-4641-a055-0f6aa9848e8f">If a CX user is par=
t of the target audience for a planned maintenance then the banners will be=
 displayed to users even if system health page access is not enabled for th=
e user.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"44504a5f-8e3e-4993-91cb-23edc00b8dd2">Support teams can c=
reate multiple incidents or planned maintenance for the same feature.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ca808469-dad4-449f-8684-c60a919cf561">The event title and=
 messages needs to be concise even though there is no character limit becau=
se the details on the banner get truncated based on the system resolution o=
r browser magnification.&nbsp;</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"691bc865-c5cd-4127-9671-d190c45faaf2">CX users will not b=
e able to view the updated message on the banners in case they have already=
 dismissed it,</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"824b23d7-ba38-43ec-9eae-87fcd8e56a02">Support team to coo=
rdinate with F&amp;UM Product/ Product Activations teams in case of missing=
 features.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e96b3c1d-4886-4a1c-9ada-566c26d3e447">If incidents are cr=
eated targeting specific roles then support teams will need to ensure that =
their own roles are also selected to view the event.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"20ea02c3-3d9e-4f41-9ffe-1ac716aacbc9"><s>If the support c=
hanges the status as Operation and uses Update Event the event will still a=
ppear on the list and user will have to end event - Resolved</s></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b884ffb0-5c5c-437c-a2b4-88c6c516b552">For scheduled maint=
enance banners - only one banner is displayed and after dismissing first ba=
nner then the next one comes up. The oldest one would be displayed first</l=
i>
 <li data-uuid=3D"bafafe32-24a9-4f42-b82c-d724c016d20e">Time zone for event=
 creation by admins or event viewing as CX user will be basis the system ti=
me zone.</li>
</ol>
<p><br></p>
